## 4.3 Paper 3: prospective identification programme and uncertainty classes

**Classification:** one genuine source/metadata mismatch and two partial over-condensations, now repaired.

Routing item A022 and the Paper 3 Draft 0.1 change log both stated that the paper had added:

- governance-event panels;
- quasi-experimental timing designs;
- out-of-sample mechanism comparison; and
- a randomized human-in-the-loop experiment.

Neither the authoritative source nor its pre-adjudication archive copy contained those designs. This was the clearest genuine omission in Papers 1--3.

Paper 3 now contains a dedicated prospective-identification section. It specifies:

1. source-linked event panels with distinct observation, recognition, assessment, review, decision, legal-adoption, deployment, compliance, realised-pressure, and ecological-response dates;
2. event-study, difference-in-differences, synthetic-control, interrupted-time-series, and state-space intervention options selected by their assumptions, with preregistered estimands, controller sign, comparison units, pretrend/anticipation tests, spillovers, and concurrent shocks;
3. held-out comparison among environmental forcing, demographic/cohort resonance, registered institutional delay, combined, and null time-series models; and
4. a randomized human-in-the-loop simulated-resource design, with preregistered treatment rules, endpoints, safety/stopping rules, sample size, exclusions, and analysis.

Every design remains prospective. None is described as a completed experiment, causal estimate, or validation of the retrospective RAM screen or field-case search.

Routing items A008 and A028 were only partially represented. The MSE section now separates process, observation/assessment, parameter, and structural-model uncertainty. It crosses parameter draws, operating-model class, and process-noise regime rather than treating one covariance matrix as structural uncertainty. It also states that model-class worst-case, distributionally robust, and model-averaged criteria answer different questions and are not interchangeable.

No sampled-review output region, RAM null result, power calculation, case-search quantity, controller-sign qualification, or falsification condition was missing.

